## Reflection on WIL (STAR Technique)
Reflecting on the transition from Design (Phase 1) to Development (Phase 2).

> Situation:
> My WIL experience was divided into two distinct phases. I began in July with a focus on UI/UX design for Cisira School, where the priority was visual communication. In October, I transitioned to the Capaciti Accelerator, where the environment shifted to a high-pressure, technical Agile environment focused on AI development.

> Task:
> My challenge was to adapt my mindset from designer to developer. For the Cisira School project, I had to ensure the brand was aesthetically pleasing. When moving to Capaciti, I had to take those design principles and learn how to build the logic behind them using AI tools, effectively becoming a hybrid professional.

> Action:
> During the Cisira project, I mastered design tools to create the Brand Guide and Prototypes. When I moved to Capaciti, I leveraged this design background to create better user interfaces for my AI apps. While others struggled with UI, I used my Phase 1 experience to ensure my tools were user-friendly.

> Result:
> The combination of these experiences has made me a Full-Product professional. I successfully delivered a complete design package for Cisira School and a portfolio of working AI applications for Capaciti. I can now wireframe a solution and then write the code to make it work.

