## Reflection on Lessons Learnt (STAR Technique)
Reflecting on the importance of Prototyping before Building.

> Situation:
> When I started the Cisira School project, I initially wanted to jump straight into making the website. However, I realized I didn't have a clear plan. Later, at Capaciti, I saw peers trying to code AI apps without a plan, leading to messy code.

> Task:
> I needed to learn the discipline of planning. For Cisira School, this meant creating a Brand Guide and Wireframes first. I had to resist the urge to rush the process.

> Action:
> I spent July to September iterating on the Cisira prototypes. I treated the Brand Guide as a rulebook. When I moved to the Capaciti coding projects, I applied this same discipline: I would sketch the UI for my AI tools before writing a single line of code.

> Result:
> This lesson saved me significant time. By mastering wireframing during the Cisira project, my development phase at Capaciti was faster because I knew exactly what I was building. I learned that a strong design foundation makes technical execution smoother.

